import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.CuspCircleOrbitGlobalPair

/-!
# Original cusp charts on the actual global circle orbit space

The proved local Hopf coordinates descend through the original coordinate
cover to the literal global circle quotient. These maps are continuous,
open, and local homeomorphisms. Their chosen local inverses give genuine
quotient charts covering exactly the open image of the original cusp
piece. In these charts the actual fixed curve is the normal zero section,
the base cusp coordinate is the original `aβ/2`, and the original toric
overlaps are retained.

The local injectivity proof uses the actual semifree action, compact local
orbits, the original local-homeomorphism cover, and properness of the
already-proved local orbit projection. No injectivity of an entire toric
coordinate cover, global product complement, or sphere identification is
assumed or concluded.
-/
